<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
{{ site.head("Model tracker · LLM Model Notes", "Recent open-weight language models from Chinese labs with architecture and license facts checked on each model repository.", "/models.html") }}
<body>
  {{ site.header("models") }}
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="prose wide">
    <p class="eyebrow">Model tracker</p>
    <h1>Open-weight models from Chinese labs</h1>
    <p>Recent open-weight releases, newest repository first within each lab. Every value comes from the model's own repository: the model card, its configuration file, or its license file. A blank or general entry means the card does not state more.</p>
    <p class="activity">Checked <time datetime="2026-11-04">4 November 2026</time>. Dates are the month the repository was created, which can differ from the announcement. Read <a href="/notes/reading-an-open-weight-model-card.html">how to read a model card</a> before comparing rows.</p>

    <table>
      <caption>Open-weight releases and their stated facts</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Lab</th><th>Model</th><th>Repository created</th><th>Architecture as stated</th><th>License</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
{%- for release in releases %}
        <tr><td>{{ release.lab }}</td><td><a href="https://huggingface.co/{{ release.repo }}">{{ release.model }}</a></td><td><time datetime="{{ release.month }}">{{ release.month }}</time></td><td>{{ release.architecture }}</td><td>{{ release.license }}</td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How rows are chosen</h2>
    <p>The tracker lists general-purpose language models with public weights. It leaves out hosted-only products, image and speech models, and quantized copies. A row is added only after its facts are read on the repository; announcements and third-party summaries are not used as sources.</p>
    <p>Licenses differ inside one model family, so each row names the license of that repository. A custom license name means the terms are specific to the release and need to be read in full.</p>
{% if nginx_xhttp_model_news_enabled | default(true) | bool %}
    <p>For releases that are not yet checked here, see the automatically refreshed <a href="/news.html">news page</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
  </main>
  {{ site.footer() }}
</body>
</html>
